DOT-Portal CI/CD — Interview Preparation Notes
1. 30-Second Project Introduction
If the interviewer asks:

“Tell me about one of your CI/CD projects.”

You can start with:

“I worked on modernizing the CI/CD process for our DOT-Portal application. We migrated the application infrastructure from EC2 to Amazon EKS and moved the CI/CD pipeline from Jenkins to GitLab CI.

The new solution uses GitLab CI for the CI stages, including code quality scanning, Docker image creation, vulnerability scanning, and publishing images to Nexus. For release orchestration, we use XL-Release, which triggers the deployment workflow, and XL-Deploy handles the deployment of the containerized application to EKS using Helm.

So the overall flow is GitLab → GitLab CI → SonarQube → Docker build → Trivy → Nexus → XL-Release → XL-Deploy → EKS.

This reduced manual deployment effort, improved standardization and traceability, and allowed us to run the application on a more scalable and highly available Kubernetes platform.”

That's your elevator pitch.

