14. Why PM2?
If asked:

“PM2 is a Node.js process manager. We use it to manage the backend Node process, including process lifecycle and restart behavior.”

But remember:

In Kubernetes, Kubernetes itself should generally be responsible for container restart/self-healing.

So if asked:

“Why PM2 if you're using Kubernetes?”

A good answer is:

“PM2 was part of the existing Node.js application runtime model. In a Kubernetes-native architecture, we could evaluate whether PM2 is still necessary and simplify the container to run the Node process directly, allowing Kubernetes to handle process lifecycle and restarts.”

That's an excellent modernization observation.

